  "descripcion_html": "<br><strong>About Us</strong><p><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">STARK is a new kind of defence technology company revolutionising the way autonomous systems are deployed across multiple domains. We design, develop, and manufacture high-performance unmanned systems that are software-defined, mass-scalable, and cost-effective — providing operators with a decisive edge in contested environments.</span></p><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;text-align:justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">We are focused on delivering deployable, high-performance systems — not future promises. In a time of rising threats, STARK is bolstering the technological edge of NATO Allies and their Partners to deter aggression and defend Europe, today.</span></p></p><br><strong>About the team</strong><p><p style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:5pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Mission Simulation</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\"> is STARK’s digital proving ground — the tactical environment where our entire ecosystem of UAVs, surface vessels, and EW systems converges. The Mission Simulation team is a small, specialized group based in Munich, working closely with our platform and C2 teams to integrate all multi-domain assets into high-fidelity, Software-in-the-Loop simulators.</span></p><p style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">We move fast, ship realistic environments, and build for three core purposes: rigorous testing, high-stakes demos, and tactical training. There is no room for gamification. We simulate the reality of combat — from complex swarm logic to EW degradation — ensuring that developers can fail fast, and real soldiers can train safely before hitting the battlefield. </span></p></p><br><strong>Your mission</strong><p><p style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align:justify;margin-top:3pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">As a Systems Integration &amp; QA Engineer, you are the critical link between our physical simulation hardware and our software development team. You will physically assemble our simulator setups and rigorously test the software environments running on them. By building our QA processes from the ground up, you ensure that every simulation runs flawlessly, and you provide highly detailed, actionable feedback to our software engineers before any system is used for high-stakes training or customer demos. </span></p></p><br><strong>Responsibilities</strong><p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\"><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Assemble</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\"> and configure physical simulator hardware setups, integrating PCs, networking gear, and tactical peripherals (e.g., VR, HOTAS) to create realistic testing environments.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Execute</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\"> comprehensive software testing within the Mission Simulation environment (e.g., VBS4, custom C++ modules) to identify bugs, performance bottlenecks, and tactical inaccuracies.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Design</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\"> and establish foundational QA testing protocols, test plans, and bug-tracking workflows from scratch.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Collaborate</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\"> directly with the software engineering team, translating simulator performance issues into clear, actionable technical feedback and bug reports.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Validate</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\"> software updates and new releases on the physical simulator setups to guarantee stability before they are deployed for customer demos or tactical training.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Reproduce</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\"> complex software and integration bugs systematically to assist developers in rapid resolution.</span></p></li></ul><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:8pt;margin-bottom:8pt;padding:0pt 0pt 1pt 0pt;\"><br></p></p><br><strong>Qualifications</strong><p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\"><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Degree in IT, Computer Science, Systems Engineering, or equivalent practical experience.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">3+ years of experience in software QA testing, system integration, or a similar role bridging IT hardware and software development.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Hands-on experience assembling IT/simulator hardware and configuring operating systems (Windows and Linux).</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Proven ability to define and build QA processes, write structured test plans, and manage bug-tracking workflows.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Strong technical communication skills to effectively translate user-end bugs into actionable data for software developers.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Professional working proficiency in English (both spoken and written).</span></p></li></ul></p><br><strong>Nice to have</strong><p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\"><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Familiarity with simulation engines (e.g., VBS4, Unreal, Unity) or complex tactical gaming environments.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Basic scripting skills (e.g., Python, PowerShell) to automate repetitive software testing or OS configuration tasks.</span></p></li><li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:'Times New Roman', serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;margin-left:-6pt;\"><p style=\"line-height:1.2;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:3pt;\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Arial, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;\">Experience in the defense sector or foundational knowledge of military operations/tactics to help evaluate simulation realism.</span></p></li></ul><br></p><p>Find <a href=\"https://www.arbeitnow.com\">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>",
